  "notes": [
    "फ़्री and बिज़ी are everyday Hindi in cities. ख़ाली (free) and व्यस्त (busy) are the Hindi words; व्यस्त sounds a little formal.",
    "कल means both \"tomorrow\" and \"yesterday\". The verb tells you which: कल मिलते हैं (tomorrow), कल मिले थे (yesterday).",
    "चलें? (\"shall we go?\") makes a friendly suggestion: कॉफ़ी पीने चलें? Over chai, it is चाय पीने चलें?",
    "सॉरी, नहीं हो पाएगा (\"sorry, it won't be possible\") is a soft way to say no. It is the same for a man and a woman."
  ]
